hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16185","He said: Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, from Yazid, from Sulayman ibn Amr ibn al-Ahwas, from his mother, she said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoning the Jamrat al-Aqabah from the belly of the valley on the day of sacrifice, saying: O people, let not some of you kill some, nor some strike some, and when you stone the Jamrah, stone it with like pebbles of khadhf. So he stoned with seven and did not stop, and behind him a man shielding him. I said: Who is this? They said: al-Fadl ibn al-Abbas."
"16186","He said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Mamar informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Sulayman ibn Amr ibn al-Ahwas, from his mother, and she pledged to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and she said: I heard the Messenger of Allah say, while stoning the Jamrah from the belly of the valley, saying: O people, let not some of you kill some, and when you see the Jamrah, stone it with like pebbles of khadhf."
"16187","He said: Rawh narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Sulayman ibn Amr ibn al-Ahwas al-Azdi, from his mother, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that she heard him say at the Jamrat al-Aqabah: O people, do not kill yourselves, and stone the Jamrah or the Jamrahs with like pebbles of khadhf. This is the end of the Musnad of the Makkis."
